se.","points":["The rook forks the king and the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","Protects the g4 pawn, which was hanging.","The next best move, 43…Qxc6, would drop Black's winning chances from 50% to 2% (+10.01).","43…Rg3+ forks the king and the pawn.","White answers 44.Kh1.","Engine line: 44.Kh1 Rh3+ 45.Kg1 Rg3+ (0.00)."]},{"ply":88,"name":"44…Rh3+","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"44…Rh3+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The rook forks the king and the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","The rook takes the half-open h-file, aiming at the king.","The next best move, 44…b5, would drop Black's winning chances from 50% to 1% (+13.72).","44…Rh3+ forks the king and the pawn and takes the half-open h-file, aiming at the king.","White answers 45.Kg1.","Engine line: 45.Kg1 Rg3+ 46.Kh2 Rh3+ (0.00)."]},{"ply":90,"name":"45…Rg3+","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"45…Rg3+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The rook forks the king and the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","Protects the g4 pawn, which was hanging.","The next best move, 45…Rh2+, would drop Black's winning chances from 50% to 1% (+13.62).","45…Rg3+ forks the king and the pawn.","White answers 46.Kh1.","Engine line: 46.Kh1 Rh3+ 47.Kg1 Rg3+ (0.00)."]}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Indian Defense: Spassky System","eco":"E14","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 10.Re1: 19 moves in all, 10 by White and 9 by Black.","Theory runs out after 10.Re1: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}